    "body": "## Motivation\n\nDiffusion host-memory planning can overcommit pinned memory when a parent cgroup has a larger limit but less remaining headroom than the child. For example, a child using 10GiB of 32GiB under a parent using 60GiB of 64GiB has 4GiB remaining, not 22GiB. Sibling usage counts against the parent.\n\n## Modifications\n\nSelect the ancestor with the least `max(0, limit - usage)` rather than the least numeric limit. Apply the existing file-cache exclusion before comparison. Extend the existing budget tests with four v1/v2 cases, including cache-adjusted headroom.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n| Check | Baseline | Candidate |\n|---|---|---|\n| Extended host-budget file | 4 failed / 32 passed | 36 passed |\n| Actual delegated cgroup v2 + 512MiB anonymous sibling | Overstates headroom and accepts a 128MiB allowance | Rejects that allowance |\n| Real SANA 600M, live nested cgroups, one streamed / 27 resident DiT blocks | Books 41,292,288 persistent pinned bytes | Keeps the streamed block pageable |\n\nBoth SANA prompts complete with pixel-identical outputs; both arms have zero OOM/OOM-kill events. Ordinary GPU-resident SANA outputs also match. No production OOM was deliberately induced. The isolated fixture releases its unused allocator/cache pages, then calibrates actual cgroup limits once; the production budget calculation is unchanged apart from this patch.\n\nSANA revision: `28f3af7689de15f3883d5863059a2fca0aa9b829` of `Efficient-Large-Model/Sana_600M_1024px_diffusers`, RTX 5090, TP=1, eager, 512×512, two prompts. **Both model arms use the same AutoencoderDC checkpoint-loading prerequisite whose root fix is already in #44690. That prerequisite is not included in this PR.** The budget unit/live-cgroup probes do not depend on that VAE correction.\n\n[Raw budget probe](https://github.com/yibol9768-alt/sglang/blob/ca72d5212b33ab079f838144467a870de749e859/validation/rtx5090-20261017/evidence/host-budget-live-cgroup.json), [nested baseline](https://github.com/yibol9768-alt/sglang/blob/ca72d5212b33ab079f838144467a870de749e859/validation/rtx5090-20261017/evidence/sana-cgroup-baseline.json), [nested candidate](https://github.com/yibol9768-alt/sglang/blob/ca72d5212b33ab079f838144467a870de749e859/validation/rtx5090-20261017/evidence/sana-cgroup-patched.json), [scripts and raw outputs](https://github.com/yibol9768-alt/sglang/blob/ca72d5212b33ab079f838144467a870de749e859/validation/rtx5090-20261017/README.md).\n\nActual unit entry points in the isolated SGLang runtime:\n\n```bash\npython test_host_budget_linux.py --baseline\npython test_host_budget_linux.py\n```\n\nThey select the respective main-source budget module and collect the changed `test_host_memory_budget.py` with real Linux dependencies. The production/source snapshots and guarded model entry points are in the linked evidence package. Runtime uses SGLang 0.5.21 compiled dependencies with relevant main Python definitions; this is not a rebuilt complete main. Relevant baseline definitions match main; upstream CI remains necessary.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo speedup is claimed. Respecting the parent budget can intentionally select the existing pageable/staged transfer fallback. The goal is to honor headroom and the existing reserve, not to change inference math. GPU validation retained 400W and a 72°C stop threshold.\n\nTargeted duplicate check: #37917 changes residency quotas, #36727 mapped offload/per-rank sharing, #37811 unified-pool residency, and #44540 HiCache physical ownership. Their inspected diffs do not change this function's binding-ancestor selection. [Pinned heads and search limits](https://github.com/yibol9768-alt/sglang/blob/ca72d5212b33ab079f838144467a870de749e859/validation/rtx5090-20261017/evidence/final-diff-audit.json).\n\nAI assistance was used for implementation, tests and this description. The human contributor reviewed the local changes and validation material before authorizing submission.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format code with pre-commit; all applicable hooks passed.\n- [x] Add focused regression tests in the existing test file.\n- [x] Documentation considered: no new public interface or invocation; behavior and limits documented here.\n- [x] Provide relevant accuracy/capacity and speed results below, with their measurement limits.\n- [x] Follow SGLang code style guidance.\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\nMaintainer review and upstream CI are requested through the normal merge-oncall/codeowner process. Local results do not replace upstream CI.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39011422962](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39011422962)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39011422823](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39011422823)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39011422740](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39011422740)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
